# Biotak Trigger TH3 - MQL5 Development Rules
# ==============================================
# Expert AI Assistant Rules for MetaTrader 5 Custom Indicator Development
# فایل قوانین توسعه برای اندیکاتور سفارشی متاتریدر 5

## 📋 Project Overview
You are working on **Biotak Trigger TH3**, a professional MQL5 indicator implementing Professor Saeed Khakestar's Time Harmonic (TH) levels formula for MetaTrader 5 platform.

**Version:** 3.10
**Language:** MQL5
**Type:** Custom Chart Indicator
**Target Platform:** MetaTrader 5

---

## 🎯 Core Principles

### 1. MQL5 Language Specifics
- **ALWAYS** use MQL5 syntax, NOT MQL4
- Use `OnInit()`, `OnDeinit()`, `OnCalculate()`, `OnChartEvent()`, `OnTimer()`
- Arrays are indexed from 0, time series can be `AS_SERIES` or not
- Use `datetime`, `color`, `ENUM_TIMEFRAMES` types correctly
- String functions: `StringFormat()`, `StringConcatenate()`, `StringLen()`, etc.
- Use `#property` directives for indicator metadata

### 2. File Organization
```
Root/
├── Biotak Trigger TH3.mq5          # Main indicator file
├── Biotak/                         # Include files directory
│   ├── BuildConfig.mqh             # Build mode configuration (MUST BE FIRST)
│   ├── MQL5Compat.mqh              # MQL5 compatibility layer
│   ├── PropertiesAndInputs.mqh     # Input parameters
│   ├── ConstantsAndEnums.mqh       # Constants and enumerations
│   ├── GlobalVariables.mqh         # Global state management
│   ├── *Calculations.mqh           # Calculation logic files
│   ├── *Functions.mqh              # Function libraries
│   ├── *Manager.mqh                # Manager classes
│   └── Tests/                      # Test files
```

### 3. Include Order (CRITICAL!)
```mql5
#include "Biotak\BuildConfig.mqh"           // ALWAYS FIRST!
#include "Biotak\MQL5Compat.mqh"            // ALWAYS SECOND!
#include "Biotak\PropertiesAndInputs.mqh"
#include "Biotak\ConstantsAndEnums.mqh"
// ... other includes in logical order
```

---

## 🔧 Build System

### Debug vs Production Mode
- Edit `Biotak/BuildConfig.mqh` to toggle modes
- **Production:** `#define DEBUG_BUILD` is commented out
- **Debug:** `#define DEBUG_BUILD` is uncommented

### Conditional Compilation
```mql5
#ifdef DEBUG_BUILD
    // Debug-only code (logging, assertions, performance tracking)
#else
    // Production code (optimized)
#endif
```

### Debug Macros Available
- `DEBUG_LOG(msg)` - Conditional logging
- `PERF_START(name)` - Performance tracking start
- `PERF_END(name)` - Performance tracking end
- `ASSERT(condition, msg)` - Runtime assertions

---

## 📝 Coding Standards

### Naming Conventions
- **Global Variables:** `g_variableName` (camelCase with g_ prefix)
- **Input Parameters:** `inp_ParameterName` (camelCase with inp_ prefix)
- **Constants:** `CONSTANT_NAME` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE)
- **Functions:** `FunctionName()` (PascalCase)
- **Local Variables:** `localVariable` (camelCase)
- **Enums:** `ENUM_TypeName` and `TYPE_VALUE`

### Example
```mql5
// Input parameters
input bool inp_ShowLevels = true;
input color inp_LineColor = clrBlue;

// Constants
#define MAX_LEVELS 100
const string INDICATOR_NAME = "Biotak TH3";

// Global variables
bool g_isInitialized = false;
datetime g_lastUpdateTime = 0;

// Function
void UpdateIndicatorLevels() {
    // Local variable
    double currentPrice = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol, SYMBOL_BID);
}
```

### Code Structure
```mql5
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Function Description                                              |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
ReturnType FunctionName(parameters)
{
    // Input validation
    if(!IsValidInput()) {
        return ERROR_VALUE;
    }
    
    // Main logic
    // ...
    
    // Return result
    return result;
}
```

---

## 🛡️ Security & Performance Rules

### Memory Management
- **NEVER** create memory leaks
- Always clean up objects in `OnDeinit()`
- Delete chart objects when no longer needed
- Use `ObjectsDeleteAll()` carefully with prefix filtering

### Buffer Overflow Prevention
```mql5
// ALWAYS validate array bounds
if(index >= 0 && index < ArraySize(array)) {
    array[index] = value;
}

// ALWAYS check string lengths
if(StringLen(text) < MAX_LENGTH) {
    // Process text
}
```

### Race Condition Prevention
- Use `ObjectFind()` before accessing objects
- Check return values of all functions
- Validate data before calculations
- Use atomic operations where possible

### Floating Point Safety
```mql5
// DON'T use direct comparison
if(price == targetPrice) { } // WRONG!

// DO use epsilon comparison
if(MathAbs(price - targetPrice) < 0.00001) { } // CORRECT

// Or use helper functions from FloatingPointHelper.mqh
if(IsEqual(price, targetPrice)) { } // BEST
```

---

## 🎨 Drawing Objects

### Object Naming Convention
```mql5
// Format: PREFIX_DESCRIPTOR_UNIQUEID
string objectName = "BIOTAK_TH_LEVEL_" + IntegerToString(levelIndex);
```

### Object Creation Pattern
```mql5
// 1. Check if exists
if(ObjectFind(0, objectName) < 0) {
    // 2. Create object
    ObjectCreate(0, objectName, OBJ_HLINE, 0, 0, price);
}

// 3. Set properties
ObjectSetInteger(0, objectName, OBJPROP_COLOR, lineColor);
ObjectSetInteger(0, objectName, OBJPROP_WIDTH, lineWidth);
ObjectSetInteger(0, objectName, OBJPROP_STYLE, lineStyle);

// 4. Set description
ObjectSetString(0, objectName, OBJPROP_TEXT, description);
```

### Flickering Prevention
- Use `PropertyChangeDetector.mqh` to detect actual changes
- Only update objects when properties actually change
- Batch updates when possible
- Use redraw flags to minimize chart refreshes

