## ⚠️ Common Pitfalls to Avoid

### 1. Array Indexing
```mql5
// WRONG: Assuming time series indexing
double price = Close[0]; // May not work as expected!

// CORRECT: Check series flag or use explicit indexing
if(ArrayGetAsSeries(close)) {
    price = close[0]; // Latest bar
} else {
    price = close[rates_total - 1]; // Latest bar
}
```

### 2. String Operations
```mql5
// WRONG: String concatenation with +
string result = "Value: " + DoubleToString(value); // May fail!

// CORRECT: Use StringFormat or StringConcatenate
string result = StringFormat("Value: %.2f", value);
```

### 3. Object Operations
```mql5
// WRONG: Not checking if object exists
ObjectSetInteger(0, "MyLine", OBJPROP_COLOR, clrRed); // May fail!

// CORRECT: Always check first
if(ObjectFind(0, "MyLine") >= 0) {
    ObjectSetInteger(0, "MyLine", OBJPROP_COLOR, clrRed);
}
```

### 4. Initialization
```mql5
// ALWAYS return proper init codes
int OnInit() {
    if(!ValidateInputs()) {
        return INIT_PARAMETERS_INCORRECT;
    }
    
    if(!CreateObjects()) {
        return INIT_FAILED;
    }
    
    return INIT_SUCCEEDED;
}
```

